From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Serve opset-28 type-only schema updates with the existing CPU kernels

conda-forge only. The newest CPU kernel of these operators is registered
open-ended, which only matches a node at exactly that schema version, so
an opset-28 model fails with "Failed to find kernel for <Op>(28)". Their
opset-28 schema only changes the type constraints, so give the existing
registrations an explicit end version of 28:

    Celu, Compress, DepthToSpace, DequantizeLinear, QuantizeLinear,
    Einsum, OneHot, Optional, OptionalHasElement, OptionalGetElement,
    ReduceLogSum, ReduceLogSumExp, ReverseSequence, Unique

The types opset 28 adds are not implemented. SpaceToDepth (new `mode`
attribute) and SwiGLU (new operator) are left alone, as are the other
execution providers. Upstream's per-operator work is in
microsoft/onnxruntime pull requests 32362, 32372, 32378, 32381 and 32393.
---
